hackmud 2020 update
Changing plans for changing times.

Hi, mudders! This goes without saying, but the world we're living in at the moment is very different to the world we lived in when we last put out an update for Hackmud. We hope that you're all well and keeping safe.

We're a small team, and life under lockdown has taken some getting used to. Even so, we're aware of the important role that videogames and other forms of entertainment are playing in our lives at the moment. We want to make sure that Hackmud remains a place that you can come to for distraction, community, mystery and memes during these tough times.

With that in mind, we have made some changes to our development structure in order to account for both the community's needs and the new circumstances we find ourselves in. As you might have noticed, we've moved away from seasonal events. In their place, we're going to begin a program of smaller but more frequent updates, starting today with a suite of improvements to Hackmud's fundamentals that should improve performance for all players.

Working in this way allows us to be more reactive to our own changing circumstances. It removes the pressure to scope and produce large, multi-faceted updates, while delivering fixes and new stuff at a steadier pace. These updates will, as ever, be free for all players. 

Thank you for bearing with us while we get back on track! It means a lot to us that you're choosing to spend your time in the MUD, and we'll do what we can to ensure that it remains a fun, rewarding, and weird place to spend your time. Stay safe, wash your hands, and run scripts.get_level!

